## API reference

### ChatAssistant

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `title:` | `String` | `"Assistant"` | Name shown in the header. |
| `action:` | `String` | - | Where the composer posts. Without it the block runs a demo. |
| `method:` | `Symbol` | `:post` | Form method. |
| `status:` | `:online`, `:offline` | `:online` | Badge state; offline disables the composer. |
| `messages_id:` | `String` | generated | Id of the messages list - the Turbo Stream target. |
| `demo_replies:` | `Array<String>` | `[]` | Canned answers for demo mode. |

Other attributes go to the card; `class:` is merged (set width and height here).

### Parts

| Part | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ChatHeader(title:, icon: :sparkles)` | Avatar with an online badge, and the name. |
| `ChatMessages` | The scrolling `role="log"` list. |
| `ChatMessage(from: :user / :assistant)` | One bubble - the user's on the end side, the assistant's on the start. |
| `ChatStatus(hidden:)` | The "Generating preview" row with the sparkle spinner. |
| `ChatSuggestions([…])` / `ChatSuggestion(text)` | Chips; clicking one sends its text. |
| `ChatComposer(placeholder:, name: "message", label:, attach:, dictate:)` | The form: field, attach, dictate and send buttons. |

### Controller (`blocks--chat-assistant`)

Emits `blocks--chat-assistant:send` with `{ text }` before sending - call `preventDefault()` to handle it
yourself (e.g. over Action Cable).

## Accessibility

- The conversation is a `role="log"` polite live region, so new replies are announced.
- The composer is labelled (`label:`), and each icon button has an `aria-label`.
- The status spinner is decorative; the status text carries the meaning.
- Send stays disabled while the field is empty; Enter sends.
